rows.en:
That's why I kind of look up to him, you know.
Like, he's my ideal person.
He's just sooo cool.{p}

But everyone says he's totally uncool.
They say the worst things, like he's fat, or embarrassing, or sloppy, or grubby.
So mean, right?{p}

Oh, what the heck, I'll skip cram school.
{a} went to the trouble of calling me in, after all.
No way am I letting this chance slip by.{p}

"Huh? The school's seven wonders?"
I wondered what {a} was going to say, and out of nowhere it's the school's seven wonders.
Every school has stories like that, right?{p}

Today, dull gray clouds filled the whole sky; it could have started raining at any moment.
The wind was clammy too, clinging to my skin and refusing to let go.
Why did I have to listen to scary stories in a dim club room on a day like this? I felt really heavy-hearted.{p}

When I opened the club room door, twelve eyes turned toward me all at once.
Six boys and girls sat quietly around the large table in the middle of the room.
It was so silent that, until I opened the door, I had thought no one was there.{p}

That's all I said before I left the club room.
Even so, for a while I couldn't walk, so I leaned against the club room door.
And then...{p}

Huh? Sanae just gave me a disgusted look and walked off.
How rude.
Somehow, I'm not in the mood for cram school anymore.{p}

I wish this were some kind of joke...
There's no escaping now.
{a} is smiling and waving at me.{p}

Wrapped in white light, I'm departing for planet Pohipohi.
The Pohipohi Dance Angels...
I wonder if we'll ever come to Earth on tour someday?{p}

"Um... Senpai.
Don't you think Sanae's a little strange?
Do you know? About her mouth..."{p}

"Okay, okay.
Taguchi, enough of that silly talk.
Just listen to what I have to say."{p}

"Huh..."
{a} won't take me seriously.
"Taguchi, you know the second gym is going to be finished soon, right?"{p}

Okay, okay.
Don't get so mad.
I'll tell you about the old school building.{p}

"There you go again, just saying any old thing..."
Oops, now he's fed up with me.
And it was only a joke.{p}

With that, he shut the club room door like he was throwing me out.
Ugh, if I'd known, I would've gone to cram school.
If I get home this early, they'll find out I skipped!{p}

Let's see, maybe I'll take a walk on the way home...
It might be fun to have a look at that flower bed everyone talks about.
Um, I'm pretty sure it was behind the gym...{p}

Can't he look me in the eye when he talks?
I knew it. To him, my feelings are...
The moment I thought that!{p}

"...All right."
He's sure well prepared.
Had he been planning this from the start, assuming I'd accept?{p}

"What★
No, that won't do.
This is an order from your senior."{p}

Oh no, I've been caught already.
"Y-yes..."
I timidly looked toward the voice.{p}

Still, is this seven wonders meeting really that famous?
Thinking about that, I walked past the restroom as fast as I could.
At the bottom of the stairs, this time a woman stopped me.{p}

There's nobody in the club room.
Hmm, what was that just now?
"Well then, I've got some business to take care of, so I'll be leaving once I've set things up. You'll be all right, won't you?"{p}
